= Solution
{parent=a}

On the negative half-line, an <antiderivative> of $1/x$ is $\ln|x|$. The <fundamental theorem of calculus> therefore gives
$$
\int_{-2}^{-1}\frac{dx}{x}=\big[\ln|x|\big]_{-2}^{-1}=\ln1-\ln2=\boxed{-\ln2}.
$$
The negative sign agrees with the negative integrand throughout the interval.

= b
{parent=1}
{scope}

= Solution
{parent=b}

The <separable differential equation> gives $dy/y=-dx$, so $y=Ce^{-x}$. The <initial condition> fixes $C=2$, and hence
$$
\boxed{y(2)=2e^{-2}\approx0.270671.}
$$

